This document has two parts. Part I is the MIT Licence, which governs the
source code of BeeLink and is offered to everyone on identical terms. Part II
is the Copyright and Brand Notice, which governs everything the MIT Licence
does not: the BeeLink name, the bee mark, the artwork, the interface design and
the written copy of the application.

Part I is deliberately left in its standard, unmodified form so that BeeLink
remains genuinely open source and compatible with every other MIT project.
Part II does not restrict Part I. It states rights that are reserved because
they were never granted.


