1. SCOPE OF THE MIT GRANT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1.1  For the purposes of this project, "the Software" licensed under Part I
     means the source code of BeeLink: index.html, sw.js and
     manifest.webmanifest, together with any future source files distributed
     under the same terms.

1.2  The MIT Licence grants broad rights over that source code. It is intended
     to be, and shall be construed as, a genuine open source grant. Nothing in
     Part II narrows, conditions or revokes any permission already given in
     Part I.

1.3  Part II concerns subject matter that Part I does not license: names,
     marks, logos, illustrations, photographic renders and written copy. Those
     works are protected independently of the source code and are reserved to
     the copyright owner.

1.4  Where a file contains both source code and reserved artwork - as
     index.html does, with its inline SVG illustrations - the code may be
     reused under Part I, but the artwork may not be extracted and reused
     apart from BeeLink.

